{
  "$comment": [
    "Shared golden vectors for the barcode parser. EVERY implementation",
    "(connector/Go, relay/TypeScript, android/Kotlin) must run these and agree.",
    "If you change this file you must re-run all three test suites.",
    "",
    "outcome values:",
    "  ACCEPT        - parsed into a usable box",
    "  WRONG_BARCODE - recognised, but it is one of the other codes on the label;",
    "                  the operator must be told to scan the long SERIAL# code",
    "  REJECT        - structurally a serial-style payload but invalid; loud failure",
    "  UNKNOWN       - no parser recognised it at all",
    "",
    "fragments: a scan that is ONE FIELD of a multi-barcode label, not a whole",
    "box. Labels from Tyco, KAC and the US/UK Simplex lines carry the part",
    "number, quantity, box id, part no, date code, week no and issue no as",
    "separate barcodes, so a scan has to be placed in the right slot by shape.",
    "",
    "kind values:",
    "  PRODUCT  - the part number, nnnn-nnnn on every label seen so far",
    "  BOX      - the carton's own id: a 16-digit Simplex serial, or a Tyco",
    "             box id like HFE283 (letters then digits)",
    "  NOT_MINE - a barcode that exists on these labels but is none of the",
    "             above: part no, date code, week no, issue no, bare quantity.",
    "             Refused with a hint -- NEVER guessed into a slot, because a",
    "             week number and a quantity are the same shape and taking one",
    "             for the other puts stock wrong with nothing on screen.",
    "",
    "want: the slot the OPERATOR asked for before scanning. Absent means a",
    "blind scan, where the classifier must place the barcode by shape alone and",
    "refuses anything ambiguous. Present means the operator tapped \"scan the",
    "product number\" (or box, or quantity) first, so the slot is known and only",
    "the shape has to fit. That is what makes an 8-digit part number and a",
    "scanned quantity safe: neither can be placed by shape, both can be placed",
    "when the operator has said which field they are pointing at.",
    "",
    "An 8-digit part number is the same number as nnnn-nnnn with the dash",
    "dropped, so it is normalised to the dashed form and resolves to one product",
    "either way. It is NEVER accepted blind: 8 digits is also the shape of a",
    "date code."
  ],
  "version": 1,
